<p>The Legion undertakes a wide range of activities, researching,
exploring, reenacting, and teaching many aspects of Roman life.  The
choice of activity is driven by the members' personal interests, with
some choosing to present a public display during out events.

<h2>Military Drills and Tactics</h2>

<p>The Imperial Roman army was an outstanding combat force.  It was
well trained, armed, and provisioned, but above all, operated using
group tactics, rather than as a collection of skilled (or less
skilled) individuals.

<p>Our <i>milites</i> (soldiers) train for and demonstrate Roman
marching drill (complete with Latin commands from the
<i>centurio</i>); use of weapons including the sword, shield, and
javelin; and combat formations for advancing under fire and attacks by
cavalry.


